ic\">Near</span> and <span class=\"italic\">close</span> have the same meaning. <span class=\"italic\">Far</span> has the opposite meaning.<br><br>The expression <span class=\"italic\">too far</span> means something is very far in a negative way.<br><br>You often talk about how far something is using the time it takes to walk or drive.  A hyphen ( - ) goes between the number and the word <span class=\"italic\">minute</span> or <span class=\"italic\">hour</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "How far is it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's about 10 miles away.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's about 40-minute walk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's too far to walk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Underground is close.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Imperatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Imperatives are verbs in the base form.  You don't use a subject. <br><br>You can use Imperatives when you give directions or suggestions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Directions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Take the Tube to James Park Station.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Visit the Queen's Gallery and Royal Mews.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Walk through St. James Park.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Contact the visitors office for an application form.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Make a left at the corner.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Look at the beautiful 